<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 9.480 percent on Thursday from 9.726 percent at the previous auction on April 9.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 900 million pounds and accepted bids for 976.125. Bills worth 984.500 million pounds mature today.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: July 24, 1997 (July 9, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.480 percent (9.726)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 976.125 million (973.250 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 2,313.025 million (1,193.250 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.253-9.497 percent (9.249-10.086)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.253-10.074 percent (9.249-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 102 (174)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 254 (179)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
